> I'm running fontmatrix 0.4.2 on OpenSUSE 11.1, and I noticed that it
> does not seem to handle .ttc (TrueType Collections).  Since fontforge
> and OpenOffice.org, for example, do seem to be able to use these
> files, I'm wondering if this is a missing feature or if I might have
> some misconfiguration somewhere. 

Hi Sean,

It’s a limitation of Fontmatrix. Fontmatrix relies on the file system to 
ensure unicity of a font, thus it would be very difficult to handle type 
collections the same way as regular font files. OTOH, I’ve started to work on 
a generalized extracting mechanism which could be used in this case too.

