Good morning Alexandre (and every/anybody else out there),

Although your news feels like a cold bucket of water has been thrown on 
me, it hasn't seriously dampened my enthusiasm for Fontmatrix.  Consider 
that I, a relative newcomer to the world of Linux (but not to the world 
of Open Source software) has been able to perceive a glaring need for a 
_/*good*/_ font management application must speak to a need that is out 
there, /although/ I will also confess that since this need is so 
obvious, /why hasn't anybody else stepped up to help address this 
need?/  I am under no illusion that I am some Great Visionary who has 
perceived of something lost to everyone else.  My hubris is not that great!

You write that you are glad someone has come along to fill in for 
Pierre.  I presume that you mean Pierre Marchand, who appears to be the 
'father' of this project.  If this is so, then you do me great credit 
which I have not earned!  Yet, over the course of time, I intend to earn 
it.  Is Mssr. Marchand still among the living and has just moved on with 
his life for reasons that I do not yet comprehend, or has he gone onto 
whatever it is that awaits us all when our earthly existence is over?  
What of the other credited authors of Fontmatrix?  Have they all 
abandoned the project?  I must say that, from my perspective as a rank 
amateur and outsider, this project appears to be /so near/ to being 
perfected (if one may truly say that of any piece of software) I simply 
do not comprehend why everyone walked away.  And what of this 
overarching project, Undertype?  What is it?  How is Fontmatrix tied to 
it?  I am probably sticking my nose into something that, if I were 
wiser, I might not, but the fact of the matter is that I was born with 
the gift of curiosity.  It was encouraged in me through my childhood and 
youth, then honed by the Jesuits when I attended college.  It is one of 
my greatest gifts and one of my greatest character flaws, because I have 
never been able to apply filters of propriety to it.  Once I have the 
bit in my mouth (do you understand this idiom?) my curiosity will not be 
denied!  So when I tell you I have a morbid sense of curiosity, you may 
rely on that!

On another level entirely, will you or anyone else be able to assist me 
in completing the installation of Fontmatrix on my own system?  I do not 
expect anyone to drop everything else to come to my aid, but at the same 
time, I would like to be able to look forward to some assistance, lest I 
find myself re-inventing the wheel, so to speak.  I know you do not know 
of anyone at this moment who can (or cares to) mentor me, be my guide, 
my professor, my /sensei/, but there is another saying, perhaps you are 
familiar with it, that says: When the student is ready, the teacher will 
appear. It has proven to be true throughout my life, so I have no reason 
to doubt its veracity now!

My respect and best regards,

